WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.570
Welcome to the DesignaKnit 8
video learning series.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.400
In this tutorial,
we'll be working in Original Pattern

3
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.460
Drafting to learn
the basics of this section.

4
00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.220
Right now, all of the icons are grayed out

5
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:19.020
except for a few here because I don't have
any garment shape in my workspace shades.

6
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.000
The easiest way to get used to using this
section is to open a garment shape

7
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.940
from the Standard Garment
Styling section first.

8
00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:30.260
Let's go there and I'm going
to say open up a child's top.

9
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.960
Okay.

10
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.700
And I have a child's top ready to knit.

11
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:41.820
We can go right back to original pattern
drafting and it shows us that this is

12
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.140
the four pieces that make up
the garment shaping file.

13
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.900
All the tools that were grayed out because

14
00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:51.340
we didn't have a shape open
are now available to us.

15
00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:56.580
First, before we get to the icons,
if I click on my piece with my left mouse

16
00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:00.980
button, it becomes the active
piece which is white.

17
00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:06.290
If I use my right mouse button,
I can drag these pieces into a position

18
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.340
that I would like and I can still
see all of my garment piece.

19
00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.660
This is a sleeve.

20
00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:16.290
It has a vertical mirror on it,
which means that things that happen

21
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.100
on this side also happen
on this side as a mirror.

22
00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:23.060
If I click on this as the active point,

23
00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:27.780
it puts a little square around it in green
to remind you it's the active point.

24
00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.490
Let's put it way out here and you can see

25
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.570
that it has changed this side, but it has
also matched the changes on this side.

26
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.850
Let's say undo.

27
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.980
I can turn my vertical mirror
on and off using this icon here.

28
00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.340
Vertical and horizontal mirrors.

29
00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:47.210
Turn this off and let's go
to the front of the garment.

30
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:54.420
The next icon over is centralized piece
and this makes the current active piece

31
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.420
the largest that it possibly
can in the workspace.

32
00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:03.100
Centralize all is next and this lets you
see all of the pattern pieces

33
00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:08.100
that comprise the garment shaping
file at one time on the screen.

34
00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:11.780
Let's go back to centralized piece.

35
00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.100
This big cursor here makes
a very large cursor.

36
00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:18.730
I can come down here to the bottom.
There we go.

37
00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.100
I can come down to the bottom and it turns

38
00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:26.170
red when it is exactly lined up with that
particular part of the garment piece.

39
00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:31.980
If you look all the way over to the right,
it says that it's 0 bottom.

40
00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.320
I'd have to move over a little bit more.

41
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.220
It says it's zero for the bottom.

42
00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.610
This means that this is the point

43
00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.300
of origin and we'll get
into this in another tutorial.

44
00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.520
The next icon we want to turn big cursor

45
00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:52.300
off and we want to turn the point
numbering on these numbers are the numbers

46
00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:56.140
that define the shape
of this garment piece.

47
00:02:56.170 --> 00:03:00.610
The numbering convention is
that the numbers start at point number one

48
00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.380
at the highest point and the
leftmost point of the garment.

49
00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.420
So we have two of the highest one,

50
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.660
but this one becomes point number
one because it's to the left.

51
00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:15.540
If I click on point number eight and move
it up, it now is the highest point,

52
00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:21.100
and it becomes .1, and it numbers it all
the way around the garment clockwise.

53
00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.740
Let's say undo this.

54
00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.340
I can use the undo button up to 20 times

55
00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:29.020
instead of only once that we
had in designaknit it seven.

56
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.500
So this means that I can walk back

57
00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:36.300
for a mistake or I can roll it
back to revert it here, too.

58
00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:39.820
So if you change your mind
about your shaping it's okay.

59
00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:43.900
Now there's a folder here
which brings up shaping thumbnails.

60
00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.440
This is new to designaknit it.

61
00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:46.780
I'm going to save this.

62
00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.900
This is new to designaknit an eight.

63
00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.980
Before, you can only see stitch patterns,

64
00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:55.380
but now you can see the parts
of the thumbnails as well.

65
00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.980
This is a baby sweater.

66
00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.020
This is a baby cardigan.

67
00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.900
This is a child's top that we're
working on right now.

68
00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:07.420
The dark blue backgrounds means that these
are standard garment styling shapes.

69
00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:13.260
You can see that they are put together
and gray for the garment pieces.

70
00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:19.740
The ones like this with the very light
gray background and blue garment piece,

71
00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:23.620
means that I'm in original pattern
drafting because it's light gray.

72
00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:27.780
And these pieces were created
in original pattern drafting.

73
00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:31.460
They were never standard
garment styling pieces.

74
00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:37.540
This one here is a medium blue,
and I have four garment pieces.

75
00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:42.420
This is the child's top that we're working
on that originated from standard garment

76
00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:46.940
styling section and are now
in original pattern drafting.

77
00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.460
This waistcoat here is the same.

78
00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:54.100
It's an original pattern drafting,
but it has a standard garment styling

79
00:04:54.130 --> 00:05:00.260
piece and also two pieces that are
originated in original pattern drafting.

80
00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:06.980
This last piece over here shows the front
panel and one of the back panels

81
00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:10.540
in standard garment styling
section of the program.

82
00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.820
And it shows other pieces that are

83
00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:18.900
in blue, medium blue, that say that these
originated in original pattern drafting.

84
00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.940
We have a third kind of piece which is

85
00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.060
exact stitch layout piece
and is shown in green.

86
00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:28.260
And we'll talk about this
in a different tutorial.

87
00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:34.180
I can use my sort button,
and if you have a lot of pieces,

88
00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:40.060
you can easily sort them by age group
and by garment type, et cetera.

89
00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:43.820
I have a search button

90
00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:49.380
which allows me to search for, let's say,
just children, just adults, females,

91
00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:55.060
males, sweaters, number of pattern pieces,
text in your notes, in your

92
00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:58.740
tension and notes filed and the last
date that it was saved.

93
00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:00.700
Okay, magnifying glasses.

94
00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:04.380
Zoom out so that you can
see more shaping files.

95
00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.360
And this one zooms in so that you can

96
00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:19.000
see the shaping files closest to you.

